course: dictionary
lesson: 15742
title: Travelled: went far, or moved
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Travelled is the past tense of travel. It tells you something went from one place to another, or that something moved. «We travelled to Scotland by train.» The word tells you the family went somewhere, and the words by train tell you how they went.
explain: The second meaning is about movement, not people. «Sound travels through air.» Here travels is the present tense, so the sound moves now. The past tense works the same way: «The sound travelled through the wall.» Look for words like train, car, far or across near the word to help you.
explain: Good readers ask: who or what moved, and how far? In «My cousin has travelled to twenty countries», the word well-travelled would describe someone who has been to many places. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Travelled is the past tense of travel, so it describes something that has already happened.
fact: «Travelled» means went from one place to another, especially far away, or moved.
fact: In British English it is spelled with two l's: travelled. In American English it is often traveled.
fact: Well-travelled means someone has been to many different places.
fact: In science and maths, travelled often tells you about distance, such as how far something moved.
exercise: «We travelled to Scotland by train.» What does travelled mean here? | Ate a big meal | Stayed at home all day | Fell asleep on the sofa | *Went from one place to another
exercise: What is the past tense of travel? | travels | travel | travelling | *travelled
exercise: «Sound travelled through the wall into our room.» What does travelled mean here? | Went to sleep | *Moved from one place to another | Stayed still | Broke into pieces
test: Maya's grandma is well-travelled. What does well-travelled mean? | *Has been to many places | Has lived in one town all her life | Is always tired after a long day | Has a very fast car
test: Dad says, «We travelled 300 miles in the car today.» What does the number tell us? | *How far they went | How fast the car was painted | How heavy the car was | How many cars they saw
exam: In «The light travelled across the sky before it reached our eyes», which word tells you the light moved? | sky | *travelled | across | eyes
